    <string name="ui_home_keycodes_sub">Find the code of any key to use in layouts</string>
    <string name="ui_guide">Quick guide</string>
    <string name="ui_guide_sub">How keys, gestures, modifiers and macros work</string>
    <string name="ui_guide_text">Every key can do several things:\n\n• Tap: types its label, or sends a key combination or runs a macro (see Tap action in the key editor).\n• Long press and heavy press: a second action.\n• Swipe in a direction (Popup mode): one of up to 8 extra characters around the key.\n• Joystick mode: sliding moves the cursor, or repeats any action per step.\n• Modifier mode (Ctrl, Alt, Shift, Meta): tap once for the next key, tap twice to lock, or hold it and press other keys for shortcuts like Meta+D.\n\nTo edit a layout: Layouts → pencil icon. Tap a key to change it, swipe a key to move it.\n\nAction values you can type anywhere:\n• text, e.g. hello\n• a key code, e.g. -61 (Tab). Use the Key codes list to find codes.\n• a combination, e.g. ctrl+c or ctrl+shift+t\n• a macro, e.g. macro:selectAllCopy\n• a layout switch, e.g. layout:@EMOJI\n\nPhysical keys (volume, keyboard, remote) can be remapped in Physical buttons.</string>

